# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-12, R-10, M-15). L §5.14.1 The leg read's class: "m.leg.amount of q reads booking state, as
# a balance does: in a def no movement reaches, or an ask, after the walk; in an arrival rule, for the movement it books;
# in another movement, only in a decision that declares reads of the place the leg took from, the reader above m
# (§5.14.2). So a tax per giver on a gift is a posting that is a decision."
# tax, a decision with reads konto, is 10 % of what g took of tomek's (40.00): 4.00, taken in proportion from ania's
# 40.00 and tomek's 60.00 (scratch/exp5.py).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if w in gifts and k.owner == w.giver then 0 else 1 prorata
kind gifts: transfers
  attr giver: key persons
  attr receiver: key persons
kind tomeks: transfers
input rate: num
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input t1_day: date
input t1_amt: money PLN
input g_day: date
input g_amt: money PLN
input tax_day: date
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0
  rule t beats base = if p == tomek then 1 else 0 when m in tomeks
  rule gift beats base, t = if p == m.receiver then 1 else 0 when m in gifts
move t1: tomeks
  on t1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount t1_amt
move g: gifts
  on g_day
  attr giver = tomek
  attr receiver = ania
  leg cash from konto to konto amount g_amt
move tax: transfers
  on tax_day
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to shop amount round(g.cash.amount of tomek * rate, minor(PLN), half-even)
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of tomek, tax.cash.amount

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  t1_day = 2026-02-02
  t1_amt = 100.00 PLN
  g_day = 2026-03-01
  g_amt = 40.00 PLN
  rate = 0.1
  tax_day = 2026-03-02
=== expect
q: (38.40 PLN, 57.60 PLN, 4.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
